# tests/xml-schemas/SCHEMAS — the published XML Schemas the SAML 1.1 / 2.0,
# WS-Trust and WS-Federation documents this service emits are validated
# against (#188). One line per file:
#
#   <local file name>  <sha256 of its bytes>  <the URL it is published at>
#
# NOTHING HERE IS VENDORED. tests/tools/fetch-xml-schemas.sh downloads every
# file when the tests image is BUILT, refuses the build if a single byte
# differs from the digest, and writes catalog.xml and all.xsd beside them so
# that validation never dials the network at test time (xmllint --nonet).
# The digest is the authority, not the host — which is also why the W3C
# files are fetched over plain http: www.w3.org answers a scripted https
# request with a Cloudflare challenge (HTTP 429, 2026-09-24) and serves the
# same bytes over http. When a publisher's address refuses anyway, the
# script asks the Internet Archive for the same URL
# (https://web.archive.org/web/2024id_/<url>, the raw capture) and accepts
# its answer only if it hashes to the same digest.
#
# The local name is the published base name where that is unique, and a
# version-qualified name where two publications share one ("ws-trust.xsd").
# ws-authorization.xsd keeps the name ws-federation.xsd imports it by.

